  "notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); business-type from the proprietary funds statement Total column (p6), measure 'cash' (cash-basis statement; aligned with FY2024). Governmental balance-sheet lines from the governmental funds statement Total column (p3), as in FY2024. Per user ruling, governmental balances are recorded as fund balances (beginning 1,152,531, ending 1,017,503, p4); cash is not filled because governmental cash is printed only as separate lines (cash and cash equivalents 654,381, cash - county treasurer 44,336, certificates of deposit 318,786; see balance_sheet). Expenditures are printed by object with no function; function chosen from the fund columns (review). The only supplementary schedule (p7, all-funds budget to actual) is combined, so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental (p4) and proprietary (p6) statements; the p7 schedule is not recorded. Business-type receipts total = operating 650,139 + nonoperating 7,016 (no single printed total). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
